# Frontend Stack

## TypeScript

- Never use `any`. Prefer explicit types and `unknown` + narrowing.
- Export types from `model/types.ts` via slice `index.ts`.

## State & API

- RTK Query: extend `baseApi` from `@/shared/api` via `injectEndpoints`.
- Axios: use `axiosInstance` from `@/shared/api` only when RTK Query is not a fit.
- Keep mock data in `entities/<name>/api/` until real endpoints exist.
- Register new API slices in the store only through `baseApi` middleware/reducer.

## Forms (React Hook Form)

- Form ownership lives in the feature (`useForm` in provider/hook), not in widgets/pages.
- Pass `control`, `errors`, `handleSubmit`, `setValue`, `getValues`, `reset` via feature context/hook.
- Bind antd inputs with `Controller` — do not use `register` (antd is uncontrolled-unfriendly).
- Wrap fields in antd `Form.Item`; show RHF errors via `help` + `validateStatus={getAntdValidateStatus(...)}` from `@/shared/lib/antd`.
- Prefer Zod + `zodResolver` for new/changed forms; keep existing `Controller` `rules` only when touching a field lightly.
- Use `useWatch` for derived UI; `useFieldArray` for repeatable rows (works, parts).
- Form value types stay with the owning feature/page; map to entity payload in the feature submit handler.
- Reference: `RepairCreateProvider` + `RepairDetailsClientStep` (`Controller` + `Form.Item`).

## UI & styles

- UI kit: `antd`. Reuse existing widgets before inventing new layout.
- Styles: SCSS Modules colocated as `ComponentName.module.scss`.
- Never use inline styles.
- Import: `import styles from './ComponentName.module.scss'`.

## React

- Functional components only.
- Keep components small: one responsibility, preferably under ~100–150 lines.
- If a component grows (many blocks, conditionals, lists, steps) — decompose into child components / widgets and extract logic into `model/` hooks or context.
- UI markup stays in the component; data fetching, mapping, and submit flow go to hooks/providers.
- React Compiler is enabled — do not add `useMemo`/`useCallback` by default.
